{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens","id":1038015,"title":"Industrialization of the manufacture of Magik itens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-25T13:30:33-08:00","id":1038015,"title":"Industrialization of the manufacture of Magik itens","content":"Could you use your knowledge of Prime to create an item that weaves the patterns of Prime needed to make magikal items?<br /> <br /> Translation: can you make a magikal item that produces magikal itens?<br /> <br /> If you put effects permanently on items... And since that process is also an effect...<br /> <br /> You could be looking for my &quot;auto plant&quot; that constantly produces blasters, or my &quot;magikal furnace&quot; that turns any sword placed on it in a &quot;holy sword of celestial fire&quot;<br /> <br /> Could I make an &quot;Nodificator&quot; reactor to place inside my Ethership that sends a quintessencial bolt, thus creating Nodes? (A magikal item that open up Nodes)<br /> <br /> This kind of thing would be ridiculously powerful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:17:10-08:00","id":1038036,"title":"","content":"If you didn't have any other spheres and you tried to make, say, a hammer that could craft other things with Prime, then it would only be able to make other items into things like itself, so limited utility.<br /> Also, considering the great amount of quintessence this sort of thing requires (and depending on the rules you're using, experience points) it would be fairly expensive and not really worth your while when you could make the magic thing you wanted in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you were an Etherite with Prime 5 (or Prime 6, I can't remember which one is required to make nodes) then sure, you can build a machine that would do that sort of thing.<br /> Making a wonder that could do this would just be ridiculously difficult though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:32:11-08:00","id":1038074,"title":"","content":"Can you make a permanent Prime 4 effect in an area (so, Corr 1) that turns ANYTHING inside into quintessence?<br /> <br /> That makes me think about &quot;Cold Fusion&quot;<br /> <br /> That would solve all your problems with quintessence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T16:02:06-08:00","id":1038092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038074#post1038074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you make a permanent Prime 4 effect in an area (so, Corr 1) that turns ANYTHING inside into quintessence?<br /> <br /> That makes me think about &quot;Cold Fusion&quot;<br /> <br /> That would solve all your problems with quintessence...</div> </div> </div> </div>For that you would need Prime 5 at least in order to rend the quintessence out of all things, both living and non living. Arguably, you might need Life 5 and Matter 5 in order to transform objects and living things into quintessence.<br /> Forces 5 as well if you want to do the same thing to Forces.<br /> Spirit 4 to do this to all things spirit,<br /> and Mine 4 to do this to illusions and chimeric things.<br /> <br /> And going by Revised rules, in order to do this you'd need about 60 Quint worth of Tass and double that many successes during a ritual to pull off, all of the appropriate Resonance to avoid terrible things happening. (You wouldn't want something like this to have a Dynamic Explosive resonance for example).<br /> <br /> Also, anything that gives your players unlimited access to quintessence is potentially game breaking, so probably not a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T16:29:54-08:00","id":1038102,"title":"","content":"The Quintessence contained in nonliving objects in minimal, so you need to sacrifice sapient creatures to generate Quintessence. What else were the Nazi death camps than giant Quintessence generators for the Nephandi? With 11 million people killed, they could have potentially generated 77 million points of Quintessence. Yes, the Nephandi were defeated before they could use that Quintessence, or is that just the comfortable lies other Mages tell themselves when they wake up screaming in the middle of the night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:02:56-08:00","id":1038108,"title":"","content":"You <i>can </i>it just requires a Master of Prime. The less broken way is to create a Node and then use correspondence to implant that node into the device. Have the device feed off the node (And since you want it to act autonomously, it's gonna cost willpower unlike a normal device.) to create tass, and then shape that tass into whatever.<br /> <br /> The broken way is to use the font of paradise rote as a baseline to create a device that feeds into another device, refreshing it's quint stores whenever needed, which is then converted into tass, and then that tass is converted into things.<br /> <br /> The true ridiculousness of this is somewhat kept in check by the exponential growth of crafting times as you try to integrate more quintessence into an artifact, putting a hardcap on it's potential power and making this method much better for mass production than for megastructures.<br /> <br /> It's still insane and your ST will throw things at you if you use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:18:43-08:00","id":1038116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038092#post1038092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that you would need Prime 5 at least in order to rend the quintessence out of all things, both living and non living. Arguably, you might need Life 5 and Matter 5 in order to transform objects and living things into quintessence.<br /> Forces 5 as well if you want to do the same thing to Forces.<br /> Spirit 4 to do this to all things spirit,<br /> and Mine 4 to do this to illusions and chimeric things.<br /> <br /> And going by Revised rules, in order to do this you'd need about 60 Quint worth of Tass and double that many successes during a ritual to pull off, all of the appropriate Resonance to avoid terrible things happening. (You wouldn't want something like this to have a Dynamic Explosive resonance for example).<br /> <br /> Also, anything that gives your players unlimited access to quintessence is potentially game breaking, so probably not a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking on a magikal item, only an effect like the level Prime 4 that &quot;undo&quot; things into quintessence (deals direct aggr damage and releases the pattern into free quintessence that can be &quot;sucked&quot;, I don't know the name of this effect in english, but I do know that it is Prime 4). So, it would just be this effect, only made permanent in an area - something like the fusion energy source that Doc Octopus builds in the movie Spiderman 2 (the first sequel).<br /> <br /> I know it is something ridiculously overpowered, I'm just making mental exercises here...<br /> <br /> EDIT: it is highly unlikely that ANYONE would let players do such things... But large magikal groups might. For instance... That kind of thing would need 60 Tass and 120 successes? So what? Call for 120 Initiates/Masters of Prime from all over the globe to Concordia and place one huge &quot;quintessential recycler&quot; for use of the Mages there... Or call in for 120 high ranking operarives from the Union graduated in Prime to attend a project on Autochtonia... It's only one succes each, and if every single one brings 1 Tass is more than enough.<br /> <br /> That kind of massive collective effort is EXACTLY what made places like Mecha, Autochtonia, Concordia and Doissetep in the first place.<br /> <br /> And... If the Hermetics could teleport the hugest Chapel of the Traditions (Doissetep) to freaking Mars, I assume that all the Traditions toghether, or the Union, could do a &quot;quintessential fusion recycler reactor&quot;.<br /> <br /> But no, your players on the Front Lines probably won't even know that their bosses have one of those on Mecha or on the lunar Victoria Station<br /> <br /> Likewise, both Traditions and Union could have a &quot;Nodificator&quot; locked bellow seven keys<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: opening Nodes is Prime 5, if you find a place with strong enough ressonances, and to &quot;undo&quot; things in their basic quintessential component, you need Prime 4, no need for other spheres<br /> I have level 6 spheres as the maximum level which I created as house rules, because the levels beyond 5 on Masters of the Arts are absolutely nosense. As such, I make it so that Prime 6 can open Nodes anywhere, including objects or living beings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-25-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:28:04-08:00","id":1038123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038116#post1038116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't thinking on a magikal item, only an effect like the level Prime 4 that &quot;undo&quot; things into quintessence (deals direct aggr damage and releases the pattern into free quintessence that can be &quot;sucked&quot;, I don't know the name of this effect in english, but I do know that it is Prime 4). So, it would just be this effect, only made permanent in an area - something like the fusion energy source that Doc Octopus builds in the movie Spiderman 2 (the first sequel).<br /> <br /> I know it is something ridiculously overpowered, I'm just making mental exercises here...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can make those kinds of continuous effects. Prime 4 to rend matter (5 for life) needs to be enacted on a target with the number of successes rolled equalling the amount you can take off.<br /> To have an effect like that just hang in the air would probably mean it will extinguish itself once it's taken of its strength worth of quint.<br /> But now you have mother problem, how do you transport it? The moment anything matter moves into it, the effect will begin breaking it down into quintessence.<br /> <br /> You would probably need something like Forces 5 to transform this effect into some kind of physical energy that can be manipulated through forces magic without need of touching Matter or Life.<br /> But then that just makes the effect bigger and more prone to failure.<br /> And I would hate to be on the receiving end of a paradox backlash caused by unmaking stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:32:29-08:00","id":1038125,"title":"","content":"Honestly, tass costs aside, it's simply more efficient and easier to make things like this as a talisman/device than as a freestanding effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:52:23-08:00","id":1038130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038123#post1038123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you can make those kinds of continuous effects. Prime 4 to rend matter (5 for life) needs to be enacted on a target with the number of successes rolled equalling the amount you can take off.<br /> To have an effect like that just hang in the air would probably mean it will extinguish itself once it's taken of its strength worth of quint.<br /> But now you have mother problem, how do you transport it? The moment anything matter moves into it, the effect will begin breaking it down into quintessence.<br /> <br /> You would probably need something like Forces 5 to transform this effect into some kind of physical energy that can be manipulated through forces magic without need of touching Matter or Life.<br /> But then that just makes the effect bigger and more prone to failure.<br /> And I would hate to be on the receiving end of a paradox backlash caused by unmaking stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 4 would be the only mean to move it, since it's not really &quot;energy&quot;, but a kind of &quot;etherial black hole&quot;... Its only etherial, you can't move it with forces any more than you can transport quintessence with telekinesis.<br /> But maybe you could move it with Prime too<br /> <br /> Like I said, that's some heavy Umbral shit. On the frontlines (earth) it would no doubt go nuclear and level a city<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038125#post1038125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, tass costs aside, it's simply more efficient and easier to make things like this as a talisman/device than as a freestanding effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I considerated that option too (funny that if I make a &quot;desintegrator beam&quot; that releases AND capture the quintessence of things, or a &quot;vampiric blade&quot;, no one would consider it an absurd or over the top, because it would be just a normal magikal item).<br /> <br /> I just liked the concept of the &quot;fusion reactor&quot;.<br /> <br /> Say... Could I use Correspondence 4 with Prime 4 to <b><i>bend space itself into a magikal item</i></b> in order to achieve exactly the SAME effect?<br /> <br /> Because, if I place this effect in a Crystal that do EXACTLY the same thing in anything in an area of 2 yards around it, it would be absolutely normal for anyone....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:23:54-08:00","id":1038148,"title":"","content":"Fusion reactors are real things though, and they only convert 0.2%-0.4% of the mass of their fuel into energy. What you are talking about would be a total conversion machine, which would actually have some very strange physics behind it if it was created as a Technocratic Device (such as muon radiation, the potential for converting normal matter into muon matter, which would allow for a room temperature fusion chain reaction). Yes, you could bend space around an object, it would just disappear from existence because it would not longer be part of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:24:39-08:00","id":1038151,"title":"","content":"Another question: can I place <b><i>a piece of an effect</i></b> on a magikal item so that others could make effects that they DONT have all spheres to cast?<br /> <br /> For example: I only have Spirit 2. I dont have Prime. Could someone build me a Talisman with the Prime 3 effect &quot;steal quintessence&quot;, so that I could steal quintessence from spirits using only the effect &quot;Spirit Touch&quot; of Spirit 2 to &quot;connect&quot; my talisman to spirit and have it drain it? <br /> Or the other way around, using a Talisman with the Spirit 2 effect to let me use my Prime 3 effect to drain? <br /> <br /> Better example: can I use my Life 4 own Sphere toghether with my &quot;Turn to Steel&quot; magikal item to turn my skin into steel&quot;?<br /> <br /> I ask this because I wanna make this:<br /> <br /> <b>Trigghronometer</b> - Talisman 4 points (Time 4, Entropy 2): this device, a clock that, instead of numbers, have Tarot figures, allow the owner to put &quot;trigger conditions&quot; on his effects. So, a Mage can use Forces 5 to summon a hurricane that won't hit women, or use Spirit 4 to wake a ward against Wraiths, except those called Stephen, or create a portal with Corr 4 that only let those who say the secret password use.<br /> This item doesn't exactly &quot;do&quot; anything by itself; it simply let Mages without access to Time and Entropy at the necessary levels to put &quot;activation triggers&quot; on their own effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:29:10-08:00","id":1038154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038151#post1038151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: can I place <b><i>a piece of an effect</i></b> on a magikal item so that others could make effects that they DONT have all spheres to cast?<br /> <br /> For example: I only have Spirit 2. I dont have Prime. Could someone build me a Talisman with the Prime 3 effect &quot;steal quintessence&quot;, so that I could steal quintessence from spirits using only the effect &quot;Spirit Touch&quot; of Spirit 2 to &quot;connect&quot; my talisman to spirit and have it drain it?<br /> Or the other way around, using a Talisman with the Spirit 2 effect to let me use my Prime 3 effect to drain?<br /> <br /> Better example: can I use my Life 4 own Sphere toghether with my &quot;Turn to Steel&quot; magikal item to turn my skin into steel&quot;?<br /> <br /> I ask this because I wanna make this:<br /> <br /> <b>Trigghronometer</b> - Talisman 4 points (Time 4, Entropy 2): this device, a clock that, instead of numbers, have Tarot figures, allow the owner to put &quot;trigger conditions&quot; on his effects. So, a Mage can use Forces 5 to summon a hurricane that won't hit women, or use Spirit 4 to wake a ward against Wraiths, except those called Stephen, or create a portal with Corr 4 that only let those who say the secret password use.<br /> This item doesn't exactly &quot;do&quot; anything by itself; it simply let Mages without access to Time and Entropy at the necessary levels to put &quot;activation triggers&quot; on their own effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> RAW - No. Effects are an all or nothing thing. You can't use your spheres to affect an effect already in place, even if its your own. The best you can do is cast another effect to counter it. The same is true for Wonders.<br /> <br /> If you want to add effects on to an existing Wonder, it's about the same in terms of rolls as crafting a new Wonder. You have to exceed the rolls made on the effect before you can add more successes.<br /> <br /> Also, it can be argued that, since it's not possible for a mage to cast more than one spell at the same time, that you can only concentrate enough to use the Wonder, or craft your own effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:16:17-08:00","id":1038185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038154#post1038154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RAW - No. Effects are an all or nothing thing. You can't use your spheres to affect an effect already in place, even if its your own. The best you can do is cast another effect to counter it. The same is true for Wonders.<br /> <br /> If you want to add effects on to an existing Wonder, it's about the same in terms of rolls as crafting a new Wonder. You have to exceed the rolls made on the effect before you can add more successes.<br /> <br /> Also, it can be argued that, since it's not possible for a mage to cast more than one spell at the same time, that you can only concentrate enough to use the Wonder, or craft your own effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it can't. It's either already explicitly stated, or already explicitly waived. Charms and Artefacts take up your magic action and are essentially rotes made solid welded to foci. Talismans operate on their own principles and use a fragment of your psyche that's embedded in them (That pesky willpower cost for forging a Talisman.) to essentially grant you as many magic actions a turn as you have talismans on your person. Of course the fact that each one requires you sacrifice a permanent point of willpower for that effect, (And that the Technological variant, devices, explicitly lacks both the ability to act autonomously, and the willpower cost.) makes this a bit pesky to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:19:01-08:00","id":1038187,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> I thought as much, but I couldn't remember what the official verdict was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:25:03-08:00","id":1038191,"title":"","content":"No problem, and sorry for the snark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:13:06-08:00","id":1038229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038036#post1038036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you didn't have any other spheres and you tried to make, say, a hammer that could craft other things with Prime, then it would only be able to make other items into things like itself, so limited utility.<br /> Also, considering the great amount of quintessence this sort of thing requires (and depending on the rules you're using, experience points) it would be fairly expensive and not really worth your while when you could make the magic thing you wanted in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you were an Etherite with Prime 5 (or Prime 6, I can't remember which one is required to make nodes) then sure, you can build a machine that would do that sort of thing.<br /> Making a wonder that could do this would just be ridiculously difficult though.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I could still make a &quot;Hammer of Luck-lization&quot;, that can be used by anyone to turn any sword into a &quot;Sword of Luck&quot; (Entropy 2, extra dices to hit) if I place the Entropy 2 effect on it?<br /> <br /> Or a &quot;Blessed Furnace for Fire Ball Entraping&quot; that will turn ANY sword inside it into a &quot;Sword of Fireballs&quot; if I have forces 3?<br /> <br /> I don't think that such a thing would have a limited utility... On the contrary, a machine that manufacture plasma guns would be incredible... You won't need the constant work of several Prime Initiates to individually and manually build each blaster, you'll just spend the time and resources once to build a really expensive machine, and after that it can produce 1.000 blasters a month.<br /> <br /> That could also be used as an explanation for the inflated resources that the Union have, like a fleet of Qui La Machine floating around Space<br /> <br /> One more thing: could you create an &quot;automatic fetish (or even familiar) manufacturer&quot;? So, just take your piece of stick, take your spirit of choice, and apply the spiritual glue that your new super fetishzator produces...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:49:25-08:00","id":1038256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038229#post1038229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I could still make a &quot;Hammer of Luck-lization&quot;, that can be used by anyone to turn any sword into a &quot;Sword of Luck&quot; (Entropy 2, extra dices to hit) if I place the Entropy 2 effect on it?<br /> <br /> Or a &quot;Blessed Furnace for Fire Ball Entraping&quot; that will turn ANY sword inside it into a &quot;Sword of Fireballs&quot; if I have forces 3?<br /> <br /> I don't think that such a thing would have a limited utility... On the contrary, a machine that manufacture plasma guns would be incredible... You won't need the constant work of several Prime Initiates to individually and manually build each blaster, you'll just spend the time and resources once to build a really expensive machine, and after that it can produce 1.000 blasters a month.<br /> <br /> That could also be used as an explanation for the inflated resources that the Union have, like a fleet of Qui La Machine floating around Space<br /> <br /> One more thing: could you create an &quot;automatic fetish (or even familiar) manufacturer&quot;? So, just take your piece of stick, take your spirit of choice, and apply the spiritual glue that your new super fetishzator produces...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, your &quot;Wonder making Furnace&quot; is going to be pretty pointless from your standpoint, because it will just be capable of doing what you can already do without need of a Wonder, and other Mages would not be able to use it unless their paradigm meshed well with yours.<br /> Making it a Talisman, on the otherhand, might allow others to use it, but that's even riskier, takes way more time, and you have to lose a Perm point of WP. Then you have to roll successes to determine it's Arete level (when you fail, you have to stop at the current level, and when you botch, everything blows up and you are left with nothing, not even the materials you have yet to use). And then you get to do the normal artefact stuff to it.<br /> <br /> Also, any items designed to create items will need to have Quintessence, usually as Tass, in order to make even an enchanted toothpick. This means you'll need to give your furnace a Periapt in order to hold all this quintessence, which is an even bigger ordeal to make.<br /> RAW - Periapts require Matter 5 to make, though personally I don't see why they couldn't also be made with Prime 3. For this, you'll need 10 points of Quint in the form of Tass for every 1 point of the periapt's value. The final periapt will be able to hold 5 points of quintessence per point of value.<br /> So if you're planning on making stuff, you better find yourself a boatload of tass. And again, be careful of the resonance, overlooking that sort of thing can lead to pretty...different results.<br /> <br /> Automatic Fetish manufacturer? Do you <i>want</i> to become the Spirit World's Public Enemy Number One?<br /> <br /> And no, Familiars by their very nature are agreements made between mage and spirit. This can never be an automatic process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T03:05:43-08:00","id":1038311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038256#post1038256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, your &amp;quot;Wonder making Furnace&amp;quot; is going to be pretty pointless from your standpoint, because it will just be capable of doing what you can already do without need of a Wonder, and other Mages would not be able to use it unless their paradigm meshed well with yours.<br /> Making it a Talisman, on the otherhand, might allow others to use it, but that's even riskier, takes way more time, and you have to lose a Perm point of WP. Then you have to roll successes to determine it's Arete level (when you fail, you have to stop at the current level, and when you botch, everything blows up and you are left with nothing, not even the materials you have yet to use). And then you get to do the normal artefact stuff to it.<br /> <br /> Also, any items designed to create items will need to have Quintessence, usually as Tass, in order to make even an enchanted toothpick. This means you'll need to give your furnace a Periapt in order to hold all this quintessence, which is an even bigger ordeal to make.<br /> RAW - Periapts require Matter 5 to make, though personally I don't see why they couldn't also be made with Prime 3. For this, you'll need 10 points of Quint in the form of Tass for every 1 point of the periapt's value. The final periapt will be able to hold 5 points of quintessence per point of value.<br /> So if you're planning on making stuff, you better find yourself a boatload of tass. And again, be careful of the resonance, overlooking that sort of thing can lead to pretty...different results.<br /> <br /> Automatic Fetish manufacturer? Do you <i>want</i> to become the Spirit World's Public Enemy Number One?<br /> <br /> And no, Familiars by their very nature are agreements made between mage and spirit. This can never be an automatic process.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Familiars, yes, it is correct.<br /> <br /> About the rest however... Look, I'm not thinking on a mere player point of view. Im thinking on a faction scale... So, what do you think the Union would prefer, having a Iniciate in Prime needing to spend all his time manually manufacturing every single one of their sunglasses devices, or just making a robot that can do it, leaving said Prime adept free for other projects? Now, even if such a thing would be higly costly - like, lets say, as costly in time and Tass as 100 of their sunglasses - the Union would still find it preferable.<br /> <br /> About the costs in Tass, that's not a problem to the Union. They DO make Prime Batteries (Periapts) on regular bases, and employ those routinely. And even the Periapt creation would be facilitated by the use of automatic facilities... Otherwise the Masters of the Union would be too busy making toys instead of actually MANAGING the Union.<br /> <br /> How else could them have a fleet of thousands of Starships roaming the Deep Space if not with mostly automatic starports?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:04:34-08:00","id":1038342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038311#post1038311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Familiars, yes, it is correct.<br /> <br /> About the rest however... Look, I'm not thinking on a mere player point of view. Im thinking on a faction scale... So, what do you think the Union would prefer, having a Iniciate in Prime needing to spend all his time manually manufacturing every single one of their sunglasses devices, or just making a robot that can do it, leaving said Prime adept free for other projects? Now, even if such a thing would be higly costly - like, lets say, as costly in time and Tass as 100 of their sunglasses - the Union would still find it preferable.<br /> <br /> About the costs in Tass, that's not a problem to the Union. They DO make Prime Batteries (Periapts) on regular bases, and employ those routinely. And even the Periapt creation would be facilitated by the use of automatic facilities... Otherwise the Masters of the Union would be too busy making toys instead of actually MANAGING the Union.<br /> <br /> How else could them have a fleet of thousands of Starships roaming the Deep Space if not with mostly automatic starports?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked, I answered, you don't like the answer so you're answering it yourself, why even bother asking in the first place?<br /> Do you just want to hear people say &quot;yes, you're right, well done&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the Union, then yeah, the Syndicate mass produces stuff, especially for Iterattion X and the Progenitors. Resources are limited for the Void engineers though because they are far too costly and and aren't nearly as easy to get a return from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:39:02-08:00","id":1038362,"title":"","content":"Do they have thousands of spaceships (what book and page are you referencing)? When we look at the population of Mages, at 1:100,000 by the last official number that I am aware of, that would give a current population of 75,000. The Technocracy may be 30% of that number and the VE, as the smallest Convention, may be 1/15th of that percentage, so 2% of the overall Mage population. That would mean that there would be only 1,500 VE to pilot your thousands of spacecraft. Anyway, p. 53 of Void Engineers states that they only have 140 official spacecraft, plus a few space stations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-26-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T07:55:21-08:00","id":1038413,"title":"","content":"They probably don't have &quot;thousands&quot; of spaceships. Each Qui La Machinae it's important, but I guess they could have hundreds of ships if we count pods. However, I guess that you don't really need to be a Mage to use one of these spaceships, Devices are supposed to be usable by especially trained unenlightened Agents too.<br /> <br /> Industrializing the creation of magical devices it's a thing in the Union. Iteration X it's particulary fond of this. We know that, in MECHA, they had a factory of Hit-Marks. However, MECHA was also known to be an inhuman place that drained a point of Quintessence of all their prissioners each day or so (don't remember the period). It also had two &quot;space nodes&quot; discovered by the Void Engineers, and some at earth too. Implying that this sort of mass production magick it's ,indeed, costly.<br /> <br /> As for the use that such an &quot;automatic enchanting machine&quot; may have. Well, Hit-Marks require Master level knowledge of various Spheres to be created (Primium, human level IA). Not just every ItX member can create them, but they're in such a high demand!.<br /> So, for the Masters that can build the Marks it's easier to lend an Artifact that can do the dirty work to his apprentices, than to supervise the creation personaly (with his Arete). That way he's free to do greater things. And if the Master were to dissapear in an Umbral Storm, the Apprentices can still use the machine to create more.<br /> <br /> That's what I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:08:25-08:00","id":1038491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038342#post1038342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked, I answered, you don't like the answer so you're answering it yourself, why even bother asking in the first place?<br /> Do you just want to hear people say &amp;quot;yes, you're right, well done&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the Union, then yeah, the Syndicate mass produces stuff, especially for Iterattion X and the Progenitors. Resources are limited for the Void engineers though because they are far too costly and and aren't nearly as easy to get a return from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I sound condescending, I really dont mean to, that's a personal flaw of mine, many people get to dislike me because I lack at some level that I can't point some perception on social interactions that people find unpleasent, the worst of all is that I never know what I do that causes this. My friends are used to my excentrical behavior, and people that get to know me realizes I'm a cool guy and pleasant company, and realize that those idiotic things I say are NOT meant to be offensive... If my tone looked a little offensive, I beg your pardon, I just ask to overlook that for future references, and please let me know when I'm being a jerk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> lol that way I can improve (oh, I was far worse when I was young)<br /> <br /> That part about the VE is something that, despite being on papper, I never agreed. Who mantain all of the Union's Umbral Weapons? And who does all the transportation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:29:51-08:00","id":1038497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038491#post1038491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry if I sound condescending, I really dont mean to, that's a personal flaw of mine, many people get to dislike me because I lack at some level that I can't point some perception on social interactions that people find unpleasent, the worst of all is that I never know what I do that causes this. My friends are used to my excentrical behavior, and people that get to know me realizes I'm a cool guy and pleasant company, and realize that those idiotic things I say are NOT meant to be offensive... If my tone looked a little offensive, I beg your pardon, I just ask to overlook that for future references, and please let me know when I'm being a jerk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> lol that way I can improve (oh, I was far worse when I was young)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, it's cool. It just irks me when I see posts that are like:<br /> A: Hey, how does X work?<br /> B: X works like this.<br /> A: Wrong! X actually works like this!&quot;<br /> I know that's not what you were getting at, though it happens so often in these kinds of games that it starts to get a bit trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038491#post1038491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That part about the VE is something that, despite being on papper, I never agreed. Who mantain all of the Union's Umbral Weapons? And who does all the transportation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Void Engineers have a department called Research and Execute who are in charge of developing and maintaining the Engineer's Arsenal. Transportation will depend on where things are going and for what purpose, but pretty standard things like engine parts and standard blasters would probably be transported by low ranking Engineers who have yet to cut their teeth in combat.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, the Post Dimensional Anomaly Void Engineers are horribly underfunded and often understocked and ill-equipped to deal with many of the things they are required to deal with. They have the least funding from the Syndicate so they often have to priorities which missions get what, forcing many groups to settle with out of date tech and fewer troops. Plus, they get the least trust from NWO so admin is always slow to respond to their requests for more things. Iteration X is sympathetic for the Engineers, but tends to stay neutral to the whole body politics of it all, some still cling to the idea of The Machine while others are focused on keeping the tech coming so NWO doesn't start getting fed up with them.<br /> Their only true allies are the Progenitors, which is probably the only reason many Engineers are still alive. Though the Progenitors are a tricky group. In many ways they are the true puppet masters of the entire Technocracy as they have the one thing that all other members desire, the key to youth and prolonged life and the means to distribute it, and if a few side effects trim some of the corners of parts of the union, parts that the Progenitors consider rather in need of removal, then so be it. Of course they must be very subtle about it or NWO is going to crack down on them hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-26-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:36:14-08:00","id":1038499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038413#post1038413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably don't have &quot;thousands&quot; of spaceships. Each Qui La Machinae it's important, but I guess they could have hundreds of ships if we count pods. However, I guess that you don't really need to be a Mage to use one of these spaceships, Devices are supposed to be usable by especially trained unenlightened Agents too.<br /> <br /> Industrializing the creation of magical devices it's a thing in the Union. Iteration X it's particulary fond of this. We know that, in MECHA, they had a factory of Hit-Marks. However, MECHA was also known to be an inhuman place that drained a point of Quintessence of all their prissioners each day or so (don't remember the period). It also had two &quot;space nodes&quot; discovered by the Void Engineers, and some at earth too. Implying that this sort of mass production magick it's ,indeed, costly.<br /> <br /> As for the use that such an &quot;automatic enchanting machine&quot; may have. Well, Hit-Marks require Master level knowledge of various Spheres to be created (Primium, human level IA). Not just every ItX member can create them, but they're in such a high demand!.<br /> So, for the Masters that can build the Marks it's easier to lend an Artifact that can do the dirty work to his apprentices, than to supervise the creation personaly (with his Arete). That way he's free to do greater things. And if the Master were to dissapear in an Umbral Storm, the Apprentices can still use the machine to create more.<br /> <br /> That's what I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I don't think they use their Qui La Machine (a Battlecruiser-like flying fortress) to transportation of personal, equipment and raw resources between their strongholds... Also, there should be some lighter military vessels other than just the Qui La Machines... So... Thousands of Vessels... All of each need several Masters to build... Not to mention the facilities to build and upkeep those - Autochtonia, Mecha, the Dypson Sphere Copernicus, all those MUST have spaceports for their works<br /> <br /> Yep, Mecha 1 and 2 are prison-factories, where they place the worse reality deviants in a automaton lobotomized state, draining one quintessence of each one the prisioners a day, and those prisioners are also used as docile enslaved labor, so it's a win-win situation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, just one thing that crossed my mind - I could use a Prime 3 &quot;drain&quot; artifact to drain from spirits, but I would need to use Spirit 2 to allow my artifact to touch the spirits, and after that I could use the effect of the artifact... But that only because I can do that as 2 different effects<br /> <br /> That makes me think, could I use Time 4 and Entropy 2 (or 3, I don't know which in M20) to place triggers on OTHER effects? Or isn't that possible? Not to do a single effect... But to make ANOTHER effect having a sort of a &quot;glitch&quot;?<br /> <br /> For example: Spirit 4 to make a Ward against Wraiths. After that, I (or even another Mage), uses Time 4 and Entropy 2 to make it &quot;malfunction&quot; when wraiths named as &quot;Bob&quot; pass?<br /> <br /> Or maybe, should I (or could I) use Prime to make a kind of &quot;selective countermagik&quot;?<br /> <br /> Could I use Prime plus Entropy 2 to make &quot;selective countermagik? (Sort of like &quot;counter any magik except if the caster is wearing blue robes)<br /> <br /> That would solve my problems a lot lol<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that I came to think about, maybe that's how Primium works. Primium counter any magik... Except those of the wearer. So... Selective countermagik. I guess that could actually work, what do you guys think?<br /> <br /> And by that I just opened the door for all players to buy triggering artifacts to place conditional triggers on all the effects of initial chars hehe (that also would bolst A LOT the Mage population in general, since I think such items would be in high demand, and probably would become far more common than normaly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-26-2017, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:45:20-08:00","id":1038504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038499#post1038499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, I don't think they use their Qui La Machine (a Battlecruiser-like flying fortress) to transportation of personal, equipment and raw resources between their strongholds... Also, there should be some lighter military vessels other than just the Qui La Machines... So... Thousands of Vessels... All of each need several Masters to build... Not to mention the facilities to build and upkeep those - Autochtonia, Mecha, the Dypson Sphere Copernicus, all those MUST have spaceports for their works<br /> <br /> Yep, Mecha 1 and 2 are prison-factories, where they place the worse reality deviants in a automaton lobotomized state, draining one quintessence of each one the prisioners a day, and those prisioners are also used as docile enslaved labor, so it's a win-win situation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, just one thing that crossed my mind - I could use a Prime 3 &quot;drain&quot; artifact to drain from spirits, but I would need to use Spirit 2 to allow my artifact to touch the spirits, and after that I could use the effect of the artifact... But that only because I can do that as 2 different effects<br /> <br /> That makes me think, could I use Time 4 and Entropy 2 (or 3, I don't know which in M20) to place triggers on OTHER effects? Or isn't that possible? Not to do a single effect... But to make ANOTHER effect having a sort of a &quot;glitch&quot;?<br /> <br /> For example: Spirit 4 to make a Ward against Wraiths. After that, I (or even another Mage), uses Time 4 and Entropy 2 to make it &quot;malfunction&quot; when wraiths named as &quot;Bob&quot; pass?<br /> <br /> Or maybe, should I (or could I) use Prime to make a kind of &quot;selective countermagik&quot;?<br /> <br /> Could I use Prime plus Entropy 2 to make &quot;selective countermagik? (Sort of like &quot;counter any magik except if the caster is wearing blue robes)<br /> <br /> That would solve my problems a lot lol</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW: no. Magic effects are an all or nothing affair. You can't attach conditional properties to an effect already in progress, if you don't have Time 4 and Entropy 1 along with the other spheres to make your effect, then it simply cannot be done as a conditional.<br /> <br /> If you want to have Selective spells, then you don't need Entropy, but rather you need the spell to be able to determine the difference between what it is or isn't affecting. So for your &quot;Countermagic everyone who isn't wearing blue&quot; would need either Forces 1 to sense blue light, or Matter 1 to sense blue objects.<br /> For example, one of my players was having a rat problem, so they put a ban on their flat, a Corr 3 effect which would solidify space, making it impossible to walk through it, for anything of lower than Human intelligence. The full spell needed Mind 1 in order for it to sense for intelligence levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:32:26-08:00","id":1038520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038504#post1038504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RAW: no. Magic effects are an all or nothing affair. You can't attach conditional properties to an effect already in progress, if you don't have Time 4 and Entropy 1 along with the other spheres to make your effect, then it simply cannot be done as a conditional.<br /> <br /> If you want to have Selective spells, then you don't need Entropy, but rather you need the spell to be able to determine the difference between what it is or isn't affecting. So for your &quot;Countermagic everyone who isn't wearing blue&quot; would need either Forces 1 to sense blue light, or Matter 1 to sense blue objects.<br /> For example, one of my players was having a rat problem, so they put a ban on their flat, a Corr 3 effect which would solidify space, making it impossible to walk through it, for anything of lower than Human intelligence. The full spell needed Mind 1 in order for it to sense for intelligence levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't I place a countermagik effect on hold? Or... Keep an effect in a temporary &quot;disabled&quot; state until some conditions are met? For example:<br /> <br /> Blessed Lab (Entropy 5) - made permanent in a lab, gives X extra dice for Research, and sometimes, allow for an EUREKA!<br /> <br /> Now, I use my countermagik on that effect...<br /> <br /> But I put Entropy plus Time to set a condition on that countermagik. So:<br /> <br /> Dispeling Trigger (Time 4, Entropy 2, Prime 1) - counter an effect if some condition is met.<br /> <br /> So, lets say Robert blesses his lab with a permanent Entropy 5 effect.<br /> <br /> A week later, I go to his lab and dispel his effect. But I don't dispel it right away; I place a trigger for the dispel. It will be dispelled if Robert try to steal my crackers again.<br /> <br /> In the next month, Robert steal my crackers, and the blessing in his lab is gone.<br /> <br /> That's a trigger condition placed ON TOP of another effect right?<br /> <br /> Could it be done, instead of a &quot;dispeller&quot; of magik... A kind of a SUPRESSOR of magik?<br /> <br /> Could I use Prime to <i>supress</i> temporarily an effect instead of totally dispeling it?<br /> <br /> Because, if I can use countermagik in that way... I can place triggers on OTHER effects...<br /> <br /> Note, I'm not adding effects to an already existing effect... I'm using a NEW effect to &quot;manipulate&quot; another, using the control over the etherial energies that Prime confers<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> EDIT: as far as I understand, you can't make triggers without Entropy. Entropy is what will &quot;turn on or off&quot; the effect; in your example of Correspondence, you either turns on or you turn off your barrier, even with Mind 1; it would be &quot;always on&quot; or &quot;always off&quot;; to place a switch you need Entropy 2 (also, Entropy 2 is conditional by itself; effects don't have a mind on their on to &quot;sense&quot; things... So, when a rat tries to pass... Well, some &quot;random event&quot; turns the effect on to prevent it). That's at least what it is said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-26-2017, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:45:37-08:00","id":1038527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038342#post1038342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked, I answered, you don't like the answer so you're answering it yourself, why even bother asking in the first place?<br /> Do you just want to hear people say &quot;yes, you're right, well done&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the Union, then yeah, the Syndicate mass produces stuff, especially for Iterattion X and the Progenitors. Resources are limited for the Void engineers though because they are far too costly and and aren't nearly as easy to get a return from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.... Iteration X mostly builds their own stuff. They do get RESOURCES from the Syndicate, but by and large this is just above and beyond what they produce themselves. Which is one main reason why it would be a civil war if the Syndicate and VE split from the NWO and Iteration X. Because Iteration X still maintains it's own production facilities rather than relying on the syndicate. Mostly because they consider the syndicate cowards barely worthy to be in the union at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T13:59:12-08:00","id":1038566,"title":"","content":"Well, every spaceship has to have at least one Enlightened on board to command the spacecraft (Void Engineer, p. 53), though the rest of the crew can be Unenlighted. And there are not thousands of spaceships, there are hundreds, and the majority of them are shuttles. There are thirty official combat spacecraft (though the VE might have that many hidden away from the rest of the Union), 5 AUC, 5 Vaders, and 20 Qui La Machines. Even if you double that amount to account for the hidden spacecraft of the VE, you are still only talking about 10 AUC, 10 Vaders, and 40 Qui La Machines. We are talking more Star Trek levels of combat capabilities, not Star Wars levels of combat capabilities, because there just are not enough VE in existence to create, maintain, and operate more spacecraft, not when the vast majority of the VE have other duties that keep them from contributing to space exploration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:34:44-08:00","id":1038581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038015-industrialization-of-the-manufacture-of-magik-itens?p=1038566#post1038566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, every spaceship has to have at least one Enlightened on board to command the spacecraft (Void Engineer, p. 53), though the rest of the crew can be Unenlighted. And there are not thousands of spaceships, there are hundreds, and the majority of them are shuttles. There are thirty official combat spacecraft (though the VE might have that many hidden away from the rest of the Union), 5 AUC, 5 Vaders, and 20 Qui La Machines. Even if you double that amount to account for the hidden spacecraft of the VE, you are still only talking about 10 AUC, 10 Vaders, and 40 Qui La Machines. We are talking more Star Trek levels of combat capabilities, not Star Wars levels of combat capabilities, because there just are not enough VE in existence to create, maintain, and operate more spacecraft, not when the vast majority of the VE have other duties that keep them from contributing to space exploration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Macrotechnicians also construct and maintain voidcraft. Though for the most part they're restricted to conventional space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T17:33:07-08:00","id":1038657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon 